  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect reports two crashes for public iOS 1.0.1 (4): one on 2026-08-25 and one on 2026-08-29, without a usable diagnostic, incident/signature ID, or crashed-binary UUID. Exact TestFlight build 8 additionally produced two reproducible iPad share crashes on 2026-09-02; both device reports show EXC_CRASH/SIGABRT in UIPopoverPresentationController because the activity controller lacked an iPad source anchor. Commit 37c2a80 fixes that path and its native regression test passes. Protected run 33616952267 distribution-signed and candidate-byte-verified successor build 9, run 33626711140 durably materialized its exact bytes, and final trusted run 33635751765 independently reverified them. The exact IPA was delivered through Transporter and finished App Store Connect processing at 2026-09-02 18:31 +05:00. Under the owner-approved simulator runtime policy, a source-current iPadOS 18.1 XCUITest now taps Share, keeps Nimbo alive, and is corroborated by the system event `UIAVC: view did appear`; source-current iPad/widget and watch simulator builds also launch cleanly. This closes the build-9 Share regression but not production stability: a conclusive crash-free-session metric window for the released build remains missing. The gate remains blocked.', 'Obtain and symbolicate any diagnostic Apple exposes, then complete the source-current TestFlight iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'pass', 'Product/build-input authority 052d12c7dfa6411428d85205d9568462d20ff87d contains the iPad share popover-anchor fix and resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (11), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000011), and Apple 1.1.0 (9). Protected run 33616952267 passed signing and candidate-byte verification, hosted run 33626711140 durably materialized the exact package and receipt as unpublished draft 381212810, and trusted verification independently reopened and reverified every exact byte. The upload manifest is atomically 3/3 verified-current with current hashes, signing evidence, and source-bound runtime QA evidence. The prior vc10/vc1000010/build-8 set is historical-only and build 8 is explicitly failed for the iPad share path. Runtime QA does not imply store delivery, crash/Vitals clearance, review, rollout, or public availability.', 'Require the protected hosted chain to recheck the mutable draft before every later use, then bind store-delivered physical QA'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'pass', 'Legacy gate ID retained for compatibility; it now represents required Android runtime QA under the product owner''s 2026-09-03 emulator-sufficient policy. Protected run 33616952267 signed and candidate-byte-verified phone vc11 and Wear vc1000011 from authority 052d12c7dfa6411428d85205d9568462d20ff87d, run 33626711140 durably materialized their exact bytes, and trusted verification rechecked them. Exact-AAB-derived upload-key-signed vc11 passed clean General Mobile API-25 launch, live provider, Share, refresh, widget render/open, cleanup, and crash/ANR filters. Current-source hosted run 33653344467 passed API 24 phone, API 36 phone, and API 36 tablet Compose UI jobs. A clean Wear OS API 37 emulator install rendered English, Russian, and Uzbek forecast/AQI surfaces and passed 10/10 cold launches with zero matching fatal/ANR records. The dedicated General Mobile is disposable for QA; the Samsung device was not modified. This runtime pass is not Play delivery or post-delivery Vitals evidence; both remain separately fail-closed.', 'Preserve runtime coverage; separately Play-deliver phone and Wear and collect conclusive UZ Vitals'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'pass', 'Legacy gate ID retained for compatibility; it now represents required Apple runtime QA under the product owner''s 2026-09-03 simulator-sufficient policy. Build 8 is historical and failed after two reproducible iPad Share crashes. Protected run 33616952267 distribution-signed and candidate-byte-verified build 9 from authority 052d12c7dfa6411428d85205d9568462d20ff87d, run 33626711140 durably materialized its exact bytes, and final trusted verification rechecked them. A source-current Release iPadOS 18.1 simulator build of 1.1.0 (9) launched with its widget; an external XCUITest tapped `Share weather`, Nimbo remained alive, and the system log recorded `UIAVC: view did appear`. A source-current watchOS 26.5 simulator build launched and passed 10/10 cold starts; hosted iOS shared and glanceable-surface tests also pass. The deployment target remains iOS 15.0. This runtime pass is not TestFlight identity, review, public availability, or a post-release crash-free metric window; those remain separately fail-closed.', 'Preserve runtime coverage; separately complete App Store release and crash-free evidence'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. Authenticated read-only checks through 2026-09-01 05:05 Asia/Tashkent confirm that review request 14 contains only the Uzbekistan Custom Store Listing en-US and ru-RU store data and remains На рассмотрении. Managed publishing is off and the latest verified publication remains 2026-08-27. A fresh logged-out gl=UZ&hl=uz page still renders the old public title Nimbo, so approval and propagation are not claimed. This proves review submission, not approval, publication, propagation, or a later policy guarantee. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md, growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md, growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-31.md, and growth/quality/store-release-recheck-2026-09-01.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
